{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Sword</b> — And he prophesied further of many wars that shall be throughout the land upon the death of Messiah son of Joseph." "<b>My shepherd</b> — Every king of the nations whom HaShem set over the earth, and who considers himself as Elohim; therefore <i>upon the man, my associate, strike the shepherd</i> — HaShem will cut off every king, and his sheep shall be scattered. Therefore it is written in the adjacent passage joined to this one: <i>and YHWH shall be king over all the earth</i>. Yefet said: for the <i>small ones</i> [הצוערים] are the opposite of the shepherds, and they are the young of the flock; but הצוערים is an adjective-form, like <i>אובדים יצערו בניו</i>. And he did not know."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The final phrase 'ולא ידע' (and he did not know) appears to be Ibn Ezra's curt dismissal of Yefet's interpretation; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:59.914758517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}